.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-STATUS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-status - Show tunnel health


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel status <tunnel> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show tunnel health

.PP
Show current health for one durable tunnel. --watch refreshes observations at --interval; a configured route is not necessarily ready to serve traffic.

.PP
Durable tunnels retain identity, routes, connectors, and domains across client sessions. Ephemeral tunnels have a separate lifecycle. Route publication and browser HTTP access require exact authorization; TLS for browser HTTP terminates at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB--interval\fP=1s
	watch polling interval (250ms-1m)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--watch\fP[=false]
	watch for health changes


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
